export default "# A2UI v0.9 Specification Compliance\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Prompt Composer Console architecture has been verified to comply with **Google's A2UI (Agent-to-User Interface) v0.9 specification**.\n\n## What is A2UI?\n\nA2UI is an open-source specification created by Google, announced on December 15, 2025.\n\n- **Repository:** [github.com/google/A2UI](https://github.com/google/A2UI)\n- **Specification:** [a2ui.org/specification/v0.9/](https://a2ui.org/specification/v0.9/)\n- **Announcement:** [Google Developers Blog](https://developers.googleblog.com/introducing-a2ui-an-open-project-for-agent-driven-interfaces/)\n- **Current Version:** v0.9.1 (production release)\n- **License:** Apache 2.0\n\n## Core A2UI Principles\n\n### 1. Security First\n> \"A2UI is a declarative data format, not executable code.\"\n\nAgents can only render components from a pre-approved catalog, reducing risks of UI injection.\n\n### 2. LLM-Friendly and Incrementally Updateable\n> \"A flat list of components with ID references which is easy for LLMs to generate incrementally.\"\n\nEnables progressive rendering as conversations evolve.\n\n### 3. Framework-Agnostic and Portable\nThe format separates UI structure from implementation, allowing the same JSON payload to render across web components, Flutter, React, and other frameworks.\n\n---\n\n## Our Compliance\n\n### Verification Matrix\n\n| Our Implementation | A2UI v0.9 Requirement | Status |\n|--------------------|----------------------|--------|\n| LLM outputs JSON cards | \"Declarative data format, not executable code\" | ✅ |\n| Frontend has trusted components (`ConsoleCard`, `Frame29`, `PromptDashboardCanvas`) | \"Pre-approved component catalog\" | ✅ |\n| `assembleConsoleWithAI()` renders at runtime | \"Agents generate UI dynamically based on context\" | ✅ |\n| HTTP 503 error if LLM fails, no fallback HTML | Zero-trust rendering | ✅ |\n| Backend decides WHAT to show, frontend decides HOW to render | Framework-agnostic separation | ✅ |\n| Temperature = 0.0 for deterministic output | Consistent UI assembly | ✅ |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Flow\n\n```\n┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n│   FRONTEND      │     │   BACKEND       │     │   LLM SERVICE   │\n│   (React)       │     │   (FastAPI)     │     │   (DeepSeek)    │\n└────────┬────────┘     └────────┬────────┘     └────────┬────────┘\n         │                       │                       │\n         │ GET /api/ai/          │                       │\n         │ assemble-console      │                       │\n         │──────────────────────►│                       │\n         │                       │                       │\n         │                       │ Fetch sessions        │\n         │                       │ from PostgreSQL       │\n         │                       │                       │\n         │                       │ POST /chat/completions│\n         │                       │──────────────────────►│\n         │                       │                       │\n         │                       │     JSON response     │\n         │                       │◄──────────────────────│\n         │                       │                       │\n         │   { cards: [...] }    │                       │\n         │◄──────────────────────│                       │\n         │                       │                       │\n         │ Render using trusted  │                       │\n         │ component catalog     │                       │\n         │                       │                       │\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Files\n\n### Frontend\n\n| File | Location | Purpose |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| `WritingAreaIndex.tsx` | `frontend/src/pages/` | Main orchestrator, calls `assembleConsoleWithAI()` |\n| `ConsolePage.tsx` | `frontend/src/pages/` | Renders AI-assembled cards |\n| `PromptDashboardCanvas.tsx` | `frontend/src/components/` | Frame29 card grid component |\n\n### Backend\n\n| File | Location | Purpose |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| `main.py` | `backend/` | `/api/ai/assemble-console` endpoint (lines 2670-2799) |\n| `grace_gui.py` | `backend/` | `query_llm()` function, LLM provider config |\n\n---\n\n## Console Assembly Prompt\n\nThe backend sends this prompt to the LLM (from `main.py` lines 2728-2736):\n\n```python\nllm_prompt = f\"\"\"Categorize these {len(session_summaries)} prompt agents into cards.\n\nData:\n{json.dumps(session_summaries, indent=2)}\n\nCategories: Design System, Learning Module, Graphics, Writing, General\n\nOutput ONLY this JSON (no XML, no markdown):\n{{\"cards\":[{{\"id\":\"...\",\"title\":\"...\",\"category\":\"...\",\"description\":\"...\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"version\":1,\"sectionCount\":N,\"lastUsed\":\"...\",\"createdAt\":\"...\"}}],\"ai_message\":\"Welcome message\"}}\"\"\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\n| Stage | Duration | Notes |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| Frontend mount | ~0ms | React renders `WritingAreaIndex` |\n| API request sent | ~50ms | Network latency |\n| Database query | 100-500ms | Fetch up to 50 sessions |\n| **LLM API call** | **2-10s** | DeepSeek inference (dominates) |\n| JSON parsing | ~50ms | Parse LLM response |\n| Response return | ~50ms | Network latency |\n| Card rendering | 100-200ms | React renders `Frame29` |\n| **Total** | **2.5-11s** | LLM call is the bottleneck |\n\n---\n\n## Strict A2UI Philosophy\n\nThe codebase enforces strict A2UI principles through comments and code:\n\n```typescript\n// STRICT A2UI: EVERY click commands the AI - NO CACHING\n// AI ALWAYS assembles - no fallbacks\n```\n\n```python\n# NO FALLBACKS. The LLM MUST generate the response.\n# If LLM fails, this endpoint fails.\n```\n\nThis means:\n- Every console load triggers an LLM call\n- No cached/static fallback UI\n- If AI is offline, user sees error (not stale data)\n\n---\n\n## LLM Provider Configuration\n\nFrom `grace_gui.py`:\n\n```python\nMODEL_PROVIDERS = {\n    \"deepseek\": {\n        \"name\": \"DeepSeek API\",\n        \"base_url\": \"https://api.deepseek.com\",\n        \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\",  # Fast model, no reasoning overhead\n        \"enabled\": True,\n        \"priority\": 1,\n    },\n    \"nvidia_nim\": {\n        \"name\": \"NVIDIA NIM Cloud API\",\n        \"base_url\": \"https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1\",\n        \"model\": \"nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1\",\n        \"enabled\": False,  # Disabled - too slow and unreliable\n        \"priority\": 2,\n    },\n}\n\nLLM_TIMEOUT = 30  # 30s timeout - fail fast\n```\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [A2UI_IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md](./A2UI_IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md) — Surface foundation implementation\n- [A2UI_QUICK_START.md](./A2UI_QUICK_START.md) — Integration quick start guide\n- [A2UI_SURFACE_INTEGRATION.md](./A2UI_SURFACE_INTEGRATION.md) — Detailed architecture\n- [A2UI_AGENT_INTEGRATION.md](./A2UI_AGENT_INTEGRATION.md) — Agent integration patterns\n- [A2UI_PATTERN_ASSEMBLY_FRAMEWORK.md](./A2UI_PATTERN_ASSEMBLY_FRAMEWORK.md) — Assembly framework\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- **A2UI Specification:** https://a2ui.org/specification/v0.9/\n- **GitHub Repository:** https://github.com/google/A2UI\n- **Google Announcement:** https://developers.googleblog.com/introducing-a2ui-an-open-project-for-agent-driven-interfaces/\n- **Partners:** Google, CopilotKit, Flutter GenUI SDK\n\n---\n\n*Last verified: 2026-07-20*\n"